        "like": 1
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "The biggest selling point of FreezeFrame + CameraAnimation was that they worked together in terms of setting up scenes.\nThe example would be that you enabled FreezeFrame to record your movements and when you have made a clone that moves around in what you previously did on repeat by itself, you can then take your time with CameraAnimation and set up recording paths around the clones you've set up.\nThe greatest thing here is that everytime you ask your CameraAnimation to \"Play\" and record along the path you made, it will reset the positions of all clones, so you can with ease edit the camera pathway to fit in perfectly with your FreezeFrame clones. \nFreezeFrame also make you able to set up standstill clones from different avatars you have, so you can set up a scene and take pictures of it from a far afterwards, instead of having to ask multiple friends to do certain task each.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
